# Clean URLs (required)

Keep on-disk `*.html` files for GitHub Pages. **Never expose `.html` in user-facing links.**

## Two environments

| Environment | Example |
|---|---|
| Production | `https://thecurlywilloweatery.com/` |
| GitHub Pages preview | `https://collingwood-web-design.github.io/The-Curly-Willow-pages/` |

## Navigation / in-page links — path-relative (not root-relative)

Root-relative links like `href="/about-us"` break project previews (they hit `github.io/about-us` instead of `github.io/The-Curly-Willow-pages/about-us`).

| Instead of | Use |
|---|---|
| `href="/about-us"` | `href="about-us"` |
| `href="/"` | `href="./"` |
| `href="/#section"` | `href="./#section"` |
| `href="about-us.html"` | `href="about-us"` |

Same-page hashes stay `#section`. Do **not** reintroduce `.html` to fix preview issues.

## SEO metadata — always production absolute clean URLs

Canonical, Open Graph, Twitter, JSON-LD, sitemap, and `llms.txt` must use:

`https://thecurlywilloweatery.com/about-us`

Never the GitHub Pages preview host, and never `.html`.

## Assets

Leave `.css`, `.js`, images, fonts, and `.pdf` extensions alone.

## New pages

1. Add `pagename.html` on disk.
2. Link it as `href="pagename"` (path-relative).
3. SEO absolute URL: `https://thecurlywilloweatery.com/pagename`.
4. Update `sitemap.xml` / `llms.txt` with the production clean URL.
5. Keep the small head script that strips a trailing `.html` from the current path (preserves any `/The-Curly-Willow-pages/` prefix).

Helpers: `python scripts/apply-clean-urls.py --site https://thecurlywilloweatery.com`, `python scripts/apply-basepath-links.py`, `python scripts/audit-clean-urls.py --site https://thecurlywilloweatery.com`, `python scripts/preview-server.py`.
